---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { loadAll } from "../lib/github";
const apps = await loadAll();
---
<Base title="About" description="Who builds Datum, how to contribute, and the licence.">
  <section class="hero dots">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="cap">About</p>
      <h1>Tools we wanted to use ourselves.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Datum is a family of free, open-source desktop apps for engineers, scientists, researchers and analysts. Each one does one kind of technical work well, in a small and fast window that works the same way as the others.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap cols">
    <section class="card">
      <h2>Who builds it</h2>
      <p>Datum is built by Edgar Mendonca, an engineer, with Claude as a coding partner. Every app is designed in the open: each repository keeps its plans, decisions and a log of every working session in <code>docs/MEMORY.md</code>.</p>
      <p>The apps are written from scratch, with their engines in Rust and their windows in SolidJS. New versions arrive in small numbered releases and install from inside the app.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Contribute</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Found a bug or want a feature?</b> Open an issue in the app's repository:
          {apps.map((a, i) => <>{i ? ", " : " "}<a href={`https://github.com/${a.repo}/issues/new`}>{a.name}</a></>)}.
          Screenshots help a lot.</li>
        <li><b>An idea for a new Datum app?</b> <a href="https://github.com/Edgar-Mendonca/Datum/issues/new">Open an issue in the Datum repository</a>.</li>
        <li><b>Code and data.</b> Pull requests are welcome. Each repository's README explains how to build it and run the checks.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>No accounts, no subscriptions, no telemetry. Your files stay on your computer. The only network call the apps make is the update check to GitHub, and this site has no tracking or cookies.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Licence</h2>
      <p>Every Datum app is free and open source under the <a href="https://github.com/Edgar-Mendonca/Datum-Plan/blob/HEAD/LICENSE">MIT licence</a>. Third-party code and fonts are listed in each repository's <code>NOTICE</code>.</p>
      <p class="muted">The installers are not code-signed yet, so Windows may show "Windows protected your PC" on the first install: choose More info › Run anyway. Every update is checked against its SHA-256 checksum.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 48px 0 40px; }
  .lead { font-size: 18px; color: var(--text2); max-width: 40em; }
  .cols { display: grid; gap: 16px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 440px), 1fr)); padding-top: 40px; }
  h2 { font-size: 19px; }
  ul { padding-left: 18px; margin: 0; }
  li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .card p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
